  "instructions": [
    "For the paste, blitz the coconut, ginger, cumin seeds and green chilli with 200ml water until smooth.",
    "Peel and dice the carrots and potato into 1cm pieces, top the beans and cut each into three, and break the dried chilli into pieces.",
    "Heat the oil in a heavy pan on a medium heat. Add the mustard seeds, dried chilli and curry leaves and let them splutter for about 15 seconds. Add the onion and fry, stirring, for 7 to 8 minutes, until it starts to soften.",
    "Add the turmeric, carrots and potatoes, fry for a few seconds, then pour in 200ml water, cover and bring to a simmer. Cook gently for 10 minutes, add the beans and cook for 8 more minutes, until all the vegetables are tender.",
    "Add the coconut paste and black pepper, season with salt, stir and simmer for 2 minutes. Whisk the yoghurt, stir it in and simmer for 1 more minute. Garnish with coriander and serve at once with rice or paratha."
  ],
